    {
      "id": "9db57108c2357d24d8bac842c1e6773d8cf45252",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443589829,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> is there a better way to \"transfer information from tls-utiils.c to quic.c\"?\n\nThe current approach looks reasonable to me. Alternatives are possibly more fragile.\n\n> should we track the addresses reported in Preferred Address TP, too? (I don't think so, because we usually lookup connection via CID, but I would like to hear another opinion oh that)\n\nThere should not be a need to track the IP addresses, the CID should be sufficient.\n\nFWIW, the currently proposed approach looks similar to handling CIDs from the `NEW_CONNECTION_ID` frame. Both the TP and frame are mentioned here: https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-quic-transport-32#section-9.6.1",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
